WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.949 --> 00:00:14.590
Minchin disliked Sara.

2
00:00:15.431 --> 00:00:18.112
But the headmistress didn't want to make Sara unhappy.

3
00:00:19.113 --> 00:00:22.896
If that happened, Sara's rich father might take Sara out of the school.

4
00:00:23.996 --> 00:00:28.900
So the headmistress always praised Sara for her good manners and kindness to the other girls.

5
00:00:29.992 --> 00:00:32.333
She always let Sara do whatever she liked.

6
00:00:33.733 --> 00:00:36.514
And quiet Sara never did anything to break the rules.

7
00:00:38.154 --> 00:00:42.476
"Lots of things just happen by accident," Sara said to Ermengarde one day.

8
00:00:42.496 --> 00:00:46.437
"I'm just lucky that my father is kind and rich.

9
00:00:47.237 --> 00:00:49.537
I'm also lucky that I learn new things easily.

10
00:00:50.418 --> 00:00:55.039
Maybe," she went on thoughtfully, "I'm really an awful child.

11
00:00:55.719 --> 00:00:58.240
But I'll never know because I don't have any problems."

12
00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:02.523
"Lavinia doesn't have any problems, and she's horrid!"

13
00:01:02.923 --> 00:01:03.724
said Ermengarde.

14
00:01:05.185 --> 00:01:07.427
Sara rubbed her nose as she considered this.

15
00:01:08.428 --> 00:01:12.351
Then she tried to be kind by repeating something she'd heard Miss Amelia say.

16
00:01:12.371 --> 00:01:17.475
"Maybe Lavinia is horrid because she's growing so fast."

17
00:01:18.796 --> 00:01:22.099
But Sara had to admit that Lavinia was indeed horrid.

18
00:01:22.920 --> 00:01:24.942
Lavinia was also jealous of Sara.

19
00:01:26.423 --> 00:01:32.249
Before Sara came, Lavinia had been the best-dressed girl at school and Miss Minchin's favorite.

20
00:01:33.330 --> 00:01:36.771
She ruled over the older girls and scared the younger ones.

21
00:01:37.791 --> 00:01:40.892
All the girls followed her because they were afraid not to.

22
00:01:42.052 --> 00:01:43.573
But then Sara arrived.

23
00:01:44.173 --> 00:01:46.453
Although Sara was rich, she was friendly.

24
00:01:47.574 --> 00:01:51.595
And as time went on, the other girls began to follow her because they liked her.

25
00:01:52.675 --> 00:01:55.556
The youngest girls adored her because she was kind to them.

26
00:01:56.924 --> 00:02:00.407
She hosted tea parties in her room and introduced them to Emily.

27
00:02:01.467 --> 00:02:05.350
Unlike Sara, Lavinia was rarely kind to the younger girls.

28
00:02:07.792 --> 00:02:11.995
One morning Sara heard Lottie crying and shouting in the main sitting room.

29
00:02:13.576 --> 00:02:16.858
Lottie was four years old, the youngest girl at school.

30
00:02:18.179 --> 00:02:20.741
Lottie's father had spoiled her after her mother died.

31
00:02:21.582 --> 00:02:24.544
If Lottie wanted something, she cried until she got it.

32
00:02:25.480 --> 00:02:28.361
If she didn't want to do something, she threw a tantrum.

33
00:02:30.902 --> 00:02:34.183
Miss Minchin and Miss Amelia were trying to calm Lottie down.

34
00:02:34.203 --> 00:02:37.444
"Why is she upset now?"

35
00:02:37.884 --> 00:02:39.564
Miss Minchin yelled over the noise.

36
00:02:39.584 --> 00:02:45.266
"Oh oh oh," sobbed Lottie.

37
00:02:45.286 --> 00:02:48.047
"I don't have a mama."

38
00:02:49.367 --> 00:02:52.288
"Don't cry, darling," said Miss Amelia.

39
00:02:56.492 --> 00:02:56.992
"Haven't got a mama!"

40
00:02:57.012 --> 00:02:57.413
howled Lottie.

41
00:02:57.433 --> 00:03:02.357
"You only say that when you can't have your way," said Miss Minchin.

42
00:03:02.377 --> 00:03:06.261
"You really should be whipped, you naughty child."

43
00:03:07.322 --> 00:03:08.943
Lottie wailed louder than ever.

44
00:03:10.885 --> 00:03:12.486
Miss Amelia began to cry.

45
00:03:13.707 --> 00:03:18.211
Miss Minchin got so angry, she stormed out of the room and left her sister to deal with

46
00:03:18.231 --> 00:03:18.792
the problem.

47
00:03:19.853 --> 00:03:21.474
Sara was standing in the hallway.

48
00:03:21.494 --> 00:03:24.140
"Oh, Sara!"

49
00:03:24.160 --> 00:03:26.882
Miss Minchin forced herself to give Sara a nice smile.

50
00:03:26.902 --> 00:03:31.365
"I stopped because I heard Lottie," said Sara.

51
00:03:31.385 --> 00:03:33.666
"Perhaps I could help her?"

52
00:03:34.887 --> 00:03:37.208
Miss Minchin's expression changed slightly.

53
00:03:37.228 --> 00:03:42.171
"You are a clever child," she said in a sharp tone.

54
00:03:43.092 --> 00:03:44.453
Then she softened her voice.

55
00:03:44.473 --> 00:03:46.474
"Go ahead.

56
00:03:46.934 --> 00:03:49.596
You can't do any worse than my sister is doing."

57
00:03:51.724 --> 00:03:55.546
Sara entered the room and found Lottie kicking and screaming on the floor.

58
00:03:56.386 --> 00:03:59.728
Miss Amelia was bending over her, looking hot and tired.

59
00:03:59.748 --> 00:04:04.370
"Poor darling," murmured Miss Amelia a few times.

60
00:04:05.870 --> 00:04:08.992
Then she said in quite a different tone, "Stop it, Lottie!

61
00:04:09.012 --> 00:04:10.292
You're a wicked child!"

62
00:04:10.312 --> 00:04:14.854
"Miss Amelia," Sara said quietly.

63
00:04:14.874 --> 00:04:18.656
"Miss Minchin says I may try to make her stop."

64
00:04:19.868 --> 00:04:21.569
Miss Amelia turned and looked at her.

65
00:04:21.589 --> 00:04:24.550
"Oh, do you think you can?"

66
00:04:25.070 --> 00:04:25.710
she gasped.

67
00:04:27.090 --> 00:04:29.351
"Lottie is such a dreadful child."

68
00:04:29.371 --> 00:04:35.573
"If you'll quietly leave the room, I'll see what I can do," promised Sara.

69
00:04:37.814 --> 00:04:41.135
Miss Amelia slipped out, leaving the two girls alone.

70
00:04:42.215 --> 00:04:44.496
Sara said nothing and she did nothing.

71
00:04:46.908 --> 00:04:49.791
She simply sat quietly on the floor next to Lottie.

72
00:04:50.611 --> 00:04:52.353
Lottie didn't know what was going on.

73
00:04:54.134 --> 00:04:55.335
She looked up at Sara.

74
00:04:55.355 --> 00:05:02.821
"I haven't got a mama," she tried to wail.

75
00:05:02.841 --> 00:05:06.344
"Neither do I," said Sara.

76
00:05:07.445 --> 00:05:09.967
This was so surprising that Lottie sat up.

77
00:05:10.708 --> 00:05:11.929
"Where is your mama?"

78
00:05:11.949 --> 00:05:17.365
"Both our mamas are angels in heaven," Sara answered.

79
00:05:17.385 --> 00:05:19.746
"Should I tell you about heaven?"

80
00:05:20.967 --> 00:05:22.107
Lottie dried her tears.

81
00:05:22.127 --> 00:05:23.968
"Yes, please."

82
00:05:25.389 --> 00:05:31.012
Sara told her a story of a beautiful place filled with happy angels and fields of flowers.

83
00:05:31.032 --> 00:05:35.815
"But I don't have a mama here at this school!"

84
00:05:36.395 --> 00:05:37.015
said Lottie.

85
00:05:38.036 --> 00:05:39.777
Sara reached for Lottie's hand.

86
00:05:39.797 --> 00:05:42.898
"I'll be your mama," she said.

87
00:05:42.918 --> 00:05:45.580
"And Emily will be your sister."

88
00:05:46.696 --> 00:05:48.157
Lottie smiled happily.

89
00:05:48.177 --> 00:05:50.378
"Let's go tell Emily."

90
00:05:50.398 --> 00:05:55.341
"Yes, and then I'll brush your hair for you," added Sara.

91
00:05:56.482 --> 00:05:59.744
Lottie happily agreed and trotted upstairs after Sara.

92
00:06:01.044 --> 00:06:06.868
By now Lottie had completely forgotten what had first upset her—Miss Amelia had tried to brush her hair!
